<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!-- The TandemTab mark (a rounded tile split by an S-curve, a dot in each field), from TandemLogo
         (viewBox 0 0 64 64) scaled by 108/64 = 1.6875.

         A tile-shaped mark maps onto an adaptive icon differently from the old glyph: the tile itself IS the
         icon, so the launcher's own mask supplies the rounded shape and this layer bleeds to the edges. The
         green field therefore moved to @color/ic_launcher_background and only the mint field is drawn here —
         whatever the mask crops, green continues underneath.

         ⚠ The dots are pulled in to ±15 from centre rather than the mark's ±12·1.6875 = ±20.25. At the true
         position a dot reaches 42 units from centre and a circular mask (guaranteed area = the central 72dp,
         i.e. radius 36) would clip it. This is a deliberate icon-only deviation; do not "fix" it back. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#34D399"
        android:pathData="M162,-54 L108,0 C105.8,33.75 87.75,51.8 54,54 C20.25,56.2 2.2,74.25 0,108 L-54,162 L-54,-54 Z" />
    <path
